course: dictionary
lesson: 3489
title: Fangs: long, sharp teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A fang is a long, sharp, pointed tooth. Dogs, wolves and snakes have them, and so do vampires in stories. Read the words around «fang» to check its meaning: «Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs» tells you the fangs are teeth that carry poison into the prey.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The first meaning of fang is a long, pointed tooth. The second is the poison tooth of a snake, or the biting part of a spider. In «Picture a museum hall with a cat skull whose two fangs are as long as your school ruler», the fangs are plain teeth, but the context shows how long they are.
explain: Context can also warn you about danger. «Keep away from snakes and dogs that bare their fangs» means to show their teeth. When an animal bares its fangs, it is giving a warning, so you should step back and leave it alone.
fact: A fang is a long, sharp, pointed tooth.
fact: Fangs are found on dogs, wolves, snakes and vampires in stories.
fact: «Venomous» means having venom, a poison that is injected through a bite or sting.
fact: Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs, mostly to catch prey, and bite people only when frightened or stepped on.
fact: In Britain the adder is the only venomous snake.
fact: «Bare» means to show, as when a dog bares its fangs as a warning.
exercise: «Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs, mostly to catch prey.» In this sentence, what are fangs? | Lumps on the back | Little bones in the ear | *Long, sharp teeth that carry poison | Soft pads on the feet
exercise: Picture a cat skull whose two fangs are as long as your school ruler. How long are the fangs? | As long as a pencil | As long as a door | *As long as a school ruler | As long as a finger
exercise: In stories, which character is most likely to have fangs? | A cloud | *A vampire | A goldfish | A bicycle
test: «Keep away from snakes and dogs that bare their fangs.» What does bare their fangs mean? | Wag their tails happily | Drink lots of water | *Show their teeth as a warning | Fall asleep in the sun
test: «The Chinese water deer has no antlers at all; males have long fangs instead.» What do the males have instead of antlers? | *Long, pointed teeth | Thin, branching horns | Long, fluffy tails | Sharp claws on their feet
exam: In «Venomous snakes inject venom through fangs», the fangs are | *Teeth that inject poison | Eyes for seeing in the dark | Wings for flying | Tongues for tasting
